---
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
---

<Section id="mission" tone="bg" labelledBy="mission-title">
  <h2 id="mission-title">Privacy for every innovator, not just big tech.</h2>

  <div class="mv">
    <div class="mv-col">
      <p class="label">Mission</p>
      <p class="mv-lead">Verifiable privacy for every innovator, not just big tech.</p>
      <blockquote class="mv-text" data-copy-exempt>
        At Obscura, we empower individuals and innovators with cutting-edge, mathematically verifiable privacy
        solutions. Our approach integrates differential privacy, federated learning, and homomorphic encryption to
        ensure personal data remains secure while enabling ethical AI innovation.
      </blockquote>
    </div>
    <div class="mv-col">
      <p class="label">Vision</p>
      <p class="mv-lead">AI and privacy, no longer in tension.</p>
      <blockquote class="mv-text" data-copy-exempt>
        We envision a future where advanced AI and uncompromised privacy coexist harmoniously. Our goal is to create
        a world where transparency, accountability, and ethical innovation form the bedrock of digital interactions,
        fostering trust in technology.
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>

  <dl class="principles">
    <div>
      <dt>Free</dt>
      <dd>No license fees, so cost is never the reason to skip privacy.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Portable</dt>
      <dd>Works in any training pipeline, in any country.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Verifiable</dt>
      <dd>The guarantee is a mathematical bound you can check, not a promise.</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <div class="context">
    <p>
      Differential privacy already protects data at Google, Apple, Microsoft and the U.S. Census Bureau. What's
      missing is a free, integrated version for everyone else.
    </p>
    <p>
      The differential privacy market is projected to grow from $1.8B in 2025 to $6.27B in 2030, about 28.4% a year.
      <span class="source">Source: The Business Research Company, March 2026.</span>
    </p>
  </div>
</Section>

<style>
  h2 {
    max-width: 22ch;
  }
  .mv {
    margin-top: var(--s-6);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-5);
  }
  .mv-col {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-2);
    align-content: start;
  }
  .mv-lead {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: calc(var(--fs-body) * 1.1);
  }
  .mv-text {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--blue);
    padding-left: var(--s-2);
  }
  .principles {
    margin: var(--s-8) 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: var(--s-4);
  }
  .principles dt {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .principles dd {
    margin: 0.375rem 0 0;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: var(--fs-small);
  }
  .context {
    margin-top: var(--s-8);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-2);
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .context .source {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .mv {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: var(--s-8);
    }
    .principles {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: var(--s-6);
    }
    .context {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: var(--s-6);
    }
    .context p {
      max-width: none;
    }
  }
</style>
